WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.779 --> 00:00:10.019
We always hear about our qualities from people
around us who compare us with

00:00:10.019 --> 00:00:11.320
our parents.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:15.089
We find people usually saying things like,
she has got her excellent

00:00:15.089 --> 00:00:20.200
drawing skills from her dad or her beautiful
singing is inherited from her mom!

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:25.050
These are the qualities we inherit from our
parents, and which are present since

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.050
birth.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:30.630
But there are several qualities which an individual
develops in their lifetime,

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.850
depending on interests and needs.

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:36.469
Like developing certain abilities, learning
new

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:39.170
languages, and so on.

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:44.920
This happens gradually, over a period of time
as and when new interests or needs

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:45.929
are encountered.

00:00:45.929 --> 00:00:51.350
This analogy can be used to study the types
of Immunity in humans!

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:52.350
Yes!

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:56.199
We have got introduced to the two major types
of Immunity in the previous

00:00:56.199 --> 00:00:57.199
video.

00:00:57.199 --> 00:01:00.410
These are Innate and Acquired immunity.

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:05.100
Let us get into the details of
these types now!

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:09.380
We will begin our journey by learning about
the innate immunity first.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:14.050
The term
“innate” means “inborn”, or “congenital”.

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:18.600
That is, “innate” here stands for being
present since birth.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.979
So is this type of immunity present in the
organism since

00:01:21.979 --> 00:01:23.100
birth?

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.220
Yes!

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:26.861
All humans are born with an innate ability
to fight off infections.

00:01:26.861 --> 00:01:32.549
This
type of immunity is called Innate immunity.

00:01:32.549 --> 00:01:37.170
And since it is present by birth, the
type is not specific to any particular infection.

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:41.310
Rather, it is a non-specific type.

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:46.810
That means, the ability helps the body fight
various acute infections on its own.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:51.290
Now to fight the invading antigens, the system
has to be prepared with some

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:53.359
strong armed forces.

00:01:53.359 --> 00:01:54.450
Right?

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:59.060
In this case, the innate immunity has a few
components that help it perform the

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.539
necessary tasks.

00:02:00.539 --> 00:02:04.921
These include the physical barriers of the
body, physiological

00:02:04.921 --> 00:02:09.640
barriers, the cells of the immune system and
a few other important molecules.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:14.010
Let
us glance at these once!

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:16.890
The first on our list are the Physical barriers.

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:21.340
We say that innate immunity is the
one with which we are born.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:24.941
So the physical barriers will include all
the organs, or

00:02:24.941 --> 00:02:28.730
their secretions which help us fight infections.

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.830
Can you cite an example for me?

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:31.830
Yes!

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:35.940
The largest human organ, that is the SKIN,
acts as the first line of defence for

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:37.390
the human body.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:41.239
So this physical barrier is an excellent example
of the innate

00:02:41.239 --> 00:02:43.290
immunity.

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:46.830
Similar to the skin, there are several other
physical barriers like the

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:53.530
mucous coatings on the respiratory, the urogenital
and the gastrointestinal tract.

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:58.930
On similar lines, we have physiological barriers
and cellular barriers as well.

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:01.629
The
Physiological barriers include the obstacles

00:03:01.629 --> 00:03:06.710
for the foriegn invaders like, acids
present in the stomach, saliva secreted by

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:10.050
the salivary glands and many more.

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:12.420
And do we know what cellular barriers are?

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:17.349
Yes !The immune cells like the
lymphocytes and monocytes, form the cellular

00:03:17.349 --> 00:03:22.939
barriers, as the invaders have to
face them as soon as they enter the body.

00:03:22.939 --> 00:03:26.240
Now which are the other molecules that we
had mentioned?

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:29.610
Well, we know that
the immune cells are capable of producing

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:34.519
target specific proteins called
antibodies against the invaders.

00:03:34.519 --> 00:03:39.550
The various types of antibodies can be grouped
as the molecules produced for fighting off

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:40.739
the infections.

00:03:40.739 --> 00:03:46.819
Now since all the components, that is the
physical barriers, the physiological ones

00:03:46.819 --> 00:03:51.519
and the immune cells are present in our body
right since birth, they are

00:03:51.519 --> 00:03:55.120
categorised as the components of Innate immunity.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:59.879
Now that we have learnt about the innate immunity
which is the first type of

00:03:59.879 --> 00:04:03.410
immunity, let’s move ahead with the second
type.

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:06.519
The next type is Acquired immunity.

00:04:06.519 --> 00:04:12.530
Here, as the name suggests, the immunity is
acquired by the individual in due course of

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:13.530
time!

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:18.060
It is a type of immunity which is developed
over a period of time and is highly

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.530
specific in nature.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:23.610
And how does immunity develop gradually with
time?

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:27.940
I mean, we understand the
fact that we are born with some ability to

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:33.370
fight infections naturally, as it happens
in case of innate immunity.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:36.389
But how can immunity of some specific type
be

00:04:36.389 --> 00:04:37.389
developed?

00:04:37.389 --> 00:04:40.430
Let us understand that with an example!

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:44.340
People these days love to ride their bikes
without wearing a helmet.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:47.490
But that is
definitely not a safe option!

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:51.990
But if a person comes across any unfortunate
accident, then a lesson for lifetime

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:54.250
is learned from it!

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:58.600
Over a period of time, the person develops
a fear for the unfortunate happening

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:02.440
and learns how to take precautions to avoid
it!

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:04.770
Same is the case with our acquired immunity!

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:09.050
There are numerous microbes present around
us.

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:12.380
They constantly find an
opportunity to enter our body.

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:17.500
Thus, our body has to encounter numerous
pathogenic microbes constantly.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:23.940
These encounters help our body to develop
strategies to fight these invaders.

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:26.650
And
this is how immunity is developed against

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:30.090
specific pathogens that attack us!

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:31.090
And

00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:34.330
this type of immunity keeps developing over
our lifetime, as we keep

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:37.190
encountering several invaders.

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:40.880
This is nothing but Acquired immunity.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:45.220
One of the simplest examples of Acquired immunity
is that of Chicken pox

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:46.220
infection.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:50.639
The chicken pox virus will act as the antigen
and our body will

00:05:50.639 --> 00:05:53.522
synthesize antibodies against it as an immune
response.

00:05:53.522 --> 00:05:55.680
Chicken pox virus → Antigen
Body synthesizes Antibodies → Immune response

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:00.729
Our immune system has a very effective memory
also known as immunological

00:06:00.729 --> 00:06:02.160
memory!

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:06.389
So once the antibodies against that particular
virus are synthesized,

00:06:06.389 --> 00:06:10.889
then next time the body will recognize the
same antigen and destroy it, before it

00:06:10.889 --> 00:06:13.110
can cause any sought of infection.

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:16.440
This is how the acquired immunity works!

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:22.090
Now that we have got introduced to it, let
us get into the details and types of

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:27.030
Acquired immunity in the next video!

